gm-method (EntityLoader async ModelPool spawn race: set entityMeshes inside spawn callback not synchronously): EntityLoader stored an EMPTY ModelPool anchor in entityMeshes by reading modelPool._entities.get(id).root synchronously BEFORE the async spawn() populated it -- so pickEntity's raycast hit 0 entities (dead scene-click SELECT). Fix: entityMeshes.set(id, root) inside the spawn callback + on lod-changed. This one fix also unblocked gizmo-move (gated on selection). Pattern: any async resource that returns a placeholder synchronously must be registered in its completion callback, not at the call site.